I am having a little problem with keycodes and nethack...

I am using Nethack 3.1.3 on a SPARC 2 running Openwindows 3.0.
I have modified some key translations in the .Xdefaults file so
I can use the keypad arrow keys for movement.  I also defined
the Ctrl arrow keys to give me multiple movement commands
instead of typing <Shift G> before the movement key.  These
keys seem to work fine for movement, but there is a little
problem during game play.  If I go to open a door, I type
the o key, and the program then asks me for a direction.  When
I press the appropriate arrow key on the keypad, nethack does
not recognize the keypress.  I have to type a number from
the main keyboard instead of on the keypad.  Normal
movement with the arrow keys works fine, but other commands
do not work.  I am using the number_pad option.

Does anybody have any experience with this problem???

The mods I made to .Xdefaults are:

NetHack*map*translations:	#override \
			Ctrl<Key>Left: input(G) input(4) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>Right: input(G) input(6) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>Up: input(G) input(8) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>Down: input(G) input(2) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>F27: input(G) input(7) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>R13: input(G) input(1) \n\
			Ctrl<Key>F29: input(G) input(9)\n\
			Ctrl<Key>F35: input(G) input(3)\n\
			<Key>Left: input(4) \n\
			<Key>Right: input(6) \n\
			<Key>Up: input(8) \n\
			<Key>Down: input(2) \n\
			<Key>F27: input(7) \n\
			<Key>R13: input(1) \n\
			<Key>F29: input(9) \n\
			<Key>F35: input(3) \n\

